IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch01`

-- Tests for the preamble and chapter 1.  Every expected value was written from the text
-- before the file was run; unit ids (1.1, 1.5 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- The preamble creates no rule (inert, reason 1), so there is nothing to test there.

§ `Tests -- preamble and chapter 1`

§§ `1.5 -- the liberties go to freemen and their heirs`

-- 1.5: "all freemen of our kingdom ... to be had and held by them and their heirs".
#ASSERT `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
-- 1.5: the heir of a freeman holds them too.
#ASSERT `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- 1.5 names freemen and their heirs only: for anyone else the text does not say.
#ASSERT `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

§§ `1.1 to 1.2 -- the freedom of the English church`

-- 1.1-1.2: the church shall be free ... "we will that it be thus observed": an infringement is a breach.
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 1 -- the English church shall be free, with her rights entire and her liberties inviolate` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `infringe the freedom of the English church, her rights or her liberties` AT 10
-- No infringement: the prohibition stands (the text gives it no end date).
-- expect: MUST NOT `infringe the freedom of the English church, her rights or her liberties`
#TRACE `ch 1 -- the English church shall be free, with her rights entire and her liberties inviolate` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1000

§§ `1.4 -- the freedom of elections`

-- 1.4: "this we will observe": interfering with the freedom of elections is a breach.
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 1 -- the freedom of elections of the English church shall be observed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `interfere with the freedom of elections of the English church` AT 10
-- expect: MUST NOT `interfere with the freedom of elections of the English church`
#TRACE `ch 1 -- the freedom of elections of the English church shall be observed` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1000

-- assertions written: 4.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
